---
description: Core project conventions (always on)
alwaysApply: true
---
- Monorepo: pnpm workspaces + Turborepo. `packages/*` (libraries), `apps/*` (apps).
- The JSON schema is the contract. `form-schema` (Zod + types) is the single source
  of truth. Renderers consume it — never duplicate validation/logic in a renderer.
- `formVersion` is decoupled from the npm version. Changing the JSON shape = bump
  `CURRENT_FORM_VERSION` + add a migration + a migration test. Never break old JSON.
- `react` / `react-dom` / `antd` / `react-native` are peerDependencies in renderers.
- Conditional logic uses JSONLogic via `form-core`. NEVER eval() on schema rules.
- TypeScript strict, no `any` in public APIs. Small modules + barrel `index.ts`.
- Tooling: Biome (lint+format), Vitest (test), Changesets (release).
